WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.960
Speaker 1: today by talking about gay Republicans.&nbsp;
Gay Republicans at one point thought, hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.640
you know what, they're going to accept us in the&nbsp;
Republican Party. Gay marriage is now legal. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:21.360
kind of becoming a non-issue. And if we are for&nbsp;
low taxes, if we are for low regulation, if we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.880
are about Christian values, whatever that means&nbsp;
at the time that they say it within the context&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.160
of the Republican Party, the Republican Party will&nbsp;
accept us because it's moved on to other things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:40.080
And unfortunately, punctuated with last week's&nbsp;
vote against marriage equality from 157 different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:46.240
Republicans in the House of Representatives. It&nbsp;
is now abundantly clear that gay Republicans have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:52.240
failed at being integrated into the Republican&nbsp;
Party. The Republican Party is seeing a sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:59.040
of resurgence of overt homophobia. Now, it's&nbsp;
important to understand that. Overt is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:05.520
key word. The homophobia never went away from the&nbsp;
Republican Party. There was this moment after gay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:11.040
marriage was legalized and Donald Trump became the&nbsp;
Republican nominee, where Donald Trump would say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.680
he's fine with gay people and gay marriage&nbsp;
and just kind of look the other way. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.920
a non-issue. And quite frankly, on a personal&nbsp;
level, I think Trump doesn't care at all about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.600
gay marriage. I think he's just it's not even an&nbsp;
issue he really cares about. But slowly but surely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.280
and we're going to talk about this in the next&nbsp;
segment as the Christian element of the Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.920
Party has become more overtly nationalistic.&nbsp;
And by that, I don't mean they happen to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.800
Christians and they are nationalists. I mean&nbsp;
they are Christian nationalists specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:50.480
as the trans issue has gotten good, has&nbsp;
made headway in reigniting some of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:56.560
visceral cultural issues, social issues for&nbsp;
Republicans. They've sort of been drawn back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:04.080
the base, fundamental homophobia. That was&nbsp;
a critical part of the Republican Party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:11.520
for a long time. But acutely at the end of the&nbsp;
George W Bush era and during the Barack Obama era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:18.320
there has been there was a period of time on the&nbsp;
show where we would much more regularly cover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:24.720
the overt homophobia, old school homophobia from&nbsp;
the Republican Party in the Bush era and in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:32.880
Obama era of the David Pakman show, we were often&nbsp;
talking about the outrageous homophobic tirades on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.760
the floor of the House and on various talk radio&nbsp;
programs by right wing Republicans. It was a much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.320
more common thing, and in the Trump era, there&nbsp;
was far less of it. Now, I'm not saying all of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.920
sudden the Republican Party was enlightened on gay&nbsp;
rights. That's not what I'm saying at all. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.480
I'm saying is they were less overtly homophobic&nbsp;
because they moved on to other things, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:56.960
the trans issue. It's important to mention. Well,&nbsp;
very interesting article now in the Texas Tribune,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.760
we failed the gay Republicans who fought for&nbsp;
acceptance in the Texas Republican Party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.480
See little progress. Progress. Gay Republicans&nbsp;
who have fought for acceptance within the Texas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:13.280
GOP over the past three decades told the Texas&nbsp;
Tribune Progress has been excruciatingly slow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.840
That's quite an understatement. Many of them&nbsp;
have left the party, even as the number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:23.360
Log Cabin Republicans in Texas continues to grow.&nbsp;
Log Cabin Republicans is a gay Republican group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:30.240
and the article sort of tells the story&nbsp;
of how there was this period of time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:38.320
I guess we would say, after the AIDS crisis, where&nbsp;
there was the idea that, listen, we're gay, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.920
we want low taxes and we want low regulation and&nbsp;
we're Christian family values, whatever. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.040
Republican Party's a big tent, and they'll welcome&nbsp;
us probably as long as we have donor dollars. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.560
there may have been a brief period of time&nbsp;
where it seemed like that was a plausible thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:04:03.280
but it has stopped. And fundamentally what this&nbsp;
comes down to is there is a group of male, mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:11.040
wealthy white gay men who think will be accepted&nbsp;
as the good guys. As long as we more or less say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:17.520
the right things, they might not love us, but&nbsp;
they'll look the other way about being gay and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:23.520
will be part of the Trump GOP. They were never&nbsp;
really going to be welcomed into the George W&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:30.320
Bush GOP during the Obama era. It was this kind of&nbsp;
transitional phase, and then the Trump GOP might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:34.160
welcome us, but it turns out that they don't.&nbsp;
And it's a very similar thing to Caitlyn Jenner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:41.520
Caitlyn Jenner. Great. Caitlyn Jenner, Republican&nbsp;
doesn't like woke whatever. She understands that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:47.520
to mean, doesn't like liberals and all this stuff,&nbsp;
but then gets booed out of CPAC because of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:54.480
she did. Of course she did. And it would sort of&nbsp;
be funny if it wasn't tragic on multiple levels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.400
I'll tell you what, some of those levels&nbsp;
are one level on which the continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:04.960
homophobia and transphobia of the Republican Party&nbsp;
is tragic is that it's 2022. And when you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:11.920
a duopoly in the United States, there's two&nbsp;
major parties. When one of those parties in 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:18.320
remains openly transphobic and homophobic. You&nbsp;
see how retrograde and recalcitrant the country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.120
is if you look at some other countries. Every&nbsp;
country has homophobia, don't get me wrong. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.280
there are countries, including some countries&nbsp;
in Europe, some countries in South America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:33.520
to a lesser degree, with multi-party systems where&nbsp;
you might have, you know, six major parties and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:39.760
five are very much on the same page, like, listen,&nbsp;
of course, gay people can get married. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:43.920
nobody should be able to get fired for their real&nbsp;
or perceived sexual orientation. And then you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.800
got like one homophobic party in the United&nbsp;
States. We have a duopoly and one of the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:54.800
parties is still basically overtly homophobic.&nbsp;
You have some Republicans who are like, listen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.960
it's a decided issue. It's not like they're going&nbsp;
to. Scheer Gay marriage. It's not like they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.720
going to cheer. Not being able to fire people&nbsp;
because you believe that they're gay, but they'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:08.000
say it's a decided issue. And we're moving on to&nbsp;
other things. But it is very retrograde. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:14.800
one level on which it is tragic. The second level&nbsp;
on which it's tragic is the Republicans who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:20.080
gay, who are desperate to be accepted into this&nbsp;
party that just doesn't want them. And they'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:26.560
probably take their money in most cases under&nbsp;
not protest, but sort of like turning their nose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:32.560
you would say, but they're not going to like&nbsp;
it. And that's sad as well, because, listen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.360
there's nothing wrong with being gay and wanting&nbsp;
low taxes and thinking low taxes are the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.760
thing. That okay, you know, people have different&nbsp;
views about what the level of taxation should be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.560
But overall, the Republican Party is&nbsp;
this movement that's much more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:52.560
just low taxes. It's much more than just low&nbsp;
regulation. It is increasingly a fundamentalist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:59.200
Christian nationalist worldview, reactionary&nbsp;
in ways that they don't even fully understand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.640
And you'll see some examples of that later in&nbsp;
the show when we look at the new Alex Jones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:07.600
conspiracy theories that even his followers don't&nbsp;
get. But it's like it sort of sounds okay and it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:12.480
tragic on that level as well. But that's what it&nbsp;
is. And it seems at this point the movement for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:18.960
the gay Republicans to be integrated into the&nbsp;
Republican Party not going particularly well.

